erDiagram
    direction TB
    accTitle: Detectra database relationships
    accDescr: Six implemented PostgreSQL tables, selected fields, primary and foreign keys, and schema-enforced optionality. Reviewer records are stored in trusted_persons. Image-level and detection-level review links are nullable and not unique.

    cameras |o..o{ images : supplies
    images ||..o{ detections : contains
    models |o..o{ detections : produces
    trusted_persons ||..o{ human_verifications : submits
    human_verifications |o..o{ images : image_review
    human_verifications |o..o{ detections : detection_review

    cameras {
        uuid camera_id PK
        varchar location_name
        boolean enabled
    }
    images {
        uuid image_id PK
        uuid camera_id FK "nullable"
        uuid verification_id FK "nullable"
        text image_url
        integer number_detections
    }
    detections {
        uuid detection_id PK
        uuid image_id FK
        uuid model_id FK "nullable"
        uuid verification_id FK "nullable"
        varchar class_label
        numeric confidence
    }
    models {
        uuid model_id PK
        varchar version_number
    }
    trusted_persons {
        uuid trusted_person_id PK
        varchar first_name
        varchar last_name
    }
    human_verifications {
        uuid verification_id PK
        uuid verified_by_id FK
        boolean target_found
        timestamptz verified_at
    }

    %% Source: backend/database/schema.sql. Only selected fields are shown.
    %% Dotted lines are non-identifying relationships: each child has its own PK.
    %% Nullable FKs allow zero or one referenced parent; no FK is UNIQUE.
    %% trusted_persons is the implemented reviewer table, not authentication.
    %% primary_account_id has no FK; there is no implemented accounts table.
    %% images.verification_id records the latest linked review, including
    %% empty-result reviews; detections.verification_id links per-box verdicts.
    %% Image bytes are stored outside PostgreSQL; image_url references storage.
